WEBVTT

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.515
Hello?

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.021
Anybody here?

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.258
Neelix?

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.335
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.841
Happy birthday, my sweet.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.902
Happy birthday, Kes.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.105
Imagine.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.614
Two years old today.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.947
If you ask me,
you don't look a day over one.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.452
Why was everyone hiding?

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:57.013
Oh, it's an old earth custom
called a surprise party.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.556
Sorry if we startled you.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.388
No, I liked it.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.826
It was very exhilarating.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:06.924
Now, how about a glass
of my special birthday punch?

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.456
Garçon?

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.061
On the rocks or straight up?

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.232
Doctor, I'm so glad you're here.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.605
My new bartender.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.836
Handsome, isn't he?

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.606
I'm here in an official
capacity, of course...

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:22.137
in case of a medical emergency.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.308
Emergency?

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.577
Surprises have been known

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:28.849
to cause acute hyperventilation,
esophageal spasms

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.914
and in extreme cases,
even coronary arrest.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.721
One can never be too careful.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.727
No.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.595
I've completed the sensor
diagnostic, Lieutenant.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.160
All systems are
fully operational.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.503
Very good, Ensign.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.270
And I've recalibrated
the accelerometer relays.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.335
Acknowledged.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.677
Is there anything else
I can do for you, sir?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.881
I presume
this notable impatience

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.614
is due to your desire
to attend the festivities

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.951
in Holodeck 2.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.183
Yes, sir.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.158
May I remind you
that your duty shift

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.059
does not officially terminate
for another 34 minutes.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:15.434
However, I believe
the holodeck power conduits

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.527
would benefit
from a routine inspection.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:21.131
Yes, sir, I'll get right on it.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.436
All stop.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.466
Mr. Kim.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.276
What is that?

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.145
Magnify.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.321
I'm afraid
that holodeck inspection

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.756
will have to wait, Ensign.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:42.318
Wait till you taste this cake.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.796
Seven layers of Jimbalian fudge,

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:48.528
and the icing is made
from pureed I'maki nuts...

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.830
Kes' favorite.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.201
Now make a wish
and blow out the candles.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.398
Well, what do I wish for?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:57.273
Anything your petite coeur
desires, ma chérie,

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.677
and with a figure like hers,
she'll probably get it, too.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.710
Okay, I wish for...

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.445
Don't tell us.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:08.079
The wish has to be a secret
if it's going to come true.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.922
Yay!

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.790
I hate to interrupt this
tender little moment, Tommy boy,

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.959
but don't you think
it's about time we shot a rack?

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.299
In a minute.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.966
Birthday gifts are also
an Earth tradition.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.804
Oh, thank you, Tom.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.139
You didn't have to.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.010
Hey, who am I
to fly in the face of tradition?

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.151
Tom, it's beautiful.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.355
It must have cost you a week's
worth of replicator rations.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.989
Two weeks, actually,
but who's counting?

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.226
I'm just glad you like it.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.292
May I?

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.204
Oh. It's lovely.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.764
You see, it's a locket.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.400
You put little photographs
in here.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:07.573
It keeps the people you love
close to your heart.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.445
Thank you.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.780
Did you see that?

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:12.944
See what?

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.283
He...

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.948
he...

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.720
he did a lovely wrapping job,
don't you think?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.851
Bridge to Janeway.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.622
Go ahead, Lieutenant.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.597
Captain, we've encountered
an unusual phenomenon...

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.964
phenomenon... phenomenon...

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.763
phenomenon...
phenomenon...

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.738
phenomenon...

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:39.109
phenomenon...
phenomenon... phenomenon...

00:06:25.482 --> 00:06:28.110
Phenomenon... phenomenon...

00:06:28.152 --> 00:06:30.120
What is going on, Lieutenant?

00:06:30.154 --> 00:06:32.418
It might simply be
a localized malfunction,

00:06:32.456 --> 00:06:34.447
but I've never heard
anything like it.

00:06:34.491 --> 00:06:35.458
My guess is...

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.287
It's a problem
with the com system itself.

00:06:38.329 --> 00:06:40.126
Janeway to Bridge.

00:06:40.164 --> 00:06:42.132
Get down to Engineering
and run a diagnostic.

00:06:42.166 --> 00:06:44.634
I'm afraid we're going to have
to cut your party short, Kes.

00:06:44.668 --> 00:06:46.636
Stations, everyone.
Let's move.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.796
But-but...

00:06:47.838 --> 00:06:49.806
what about
the Jimbalian fudge cake?

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.775
Save me a slice, won't you?

00:06:56.647 --> 00:06:58.808
These readings indicate
the space ahead of us

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:00.111
is literally changing shape.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.109
A best guess is it's some type
of spatial distortion wave.

00:07:04.154 --> 00:07:06.418
Is the anomaly responsible
for the com system malfunction?

00:07:06.457 --> 00:07:07.617
I think so.

00:07:07.658 --> 00:07:09.785
It's generating intense pulses
of EM radiation,

00:07:09.827 --> 00:07:11.419
and if we don't

00:07:11.462 --> 00:07:13.896
it's going to intercept us
in less than ten minutes.

00:07:13.931 --> 00:07:16.764
Acknowledged.
Full reverse, Ensign.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.858
Aye, sir.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.926
We can't go backwards, either,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:07:20.037 --> 00:07:23.063
The distortion has completely
surrounded us, like a ring.

00:07:24.641 --> 00:07:25.938
If we cannot go around it,

00:07:25.976 --> 00:07:27.739
then we will have
to go through it.

00:07:27.778 --> 00:07:29.803
There's no telling
what that would do to the ship.

00:07:29.847 --> 00:07:31.542
From what you have told me,
Ensign,

00:07:31.582 --> 00:07:34.483
the distortion ring will make
contact with us momentarily

00:07:34.518 --> 00:07:36.748
whether we attempt
to pass through it or not.

00:07:36.787 --> 00:07:39.779
I prefer to minimize the amount
of time that contact lasts.

00:07:39.823 --> 00:07:41.450
Shields at maximum.

00:07:41.492 --> 00:07:44.655
Warp 3. Engage.

00:07:47.998 --> 00:07:50.466
The distortion ring
has collapsed the warp field.

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:52.230
Engines are off-line.

00:07:54.004 --> 00:07:56.802
Find the Captain
and inform her of our status.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:57.898
Yes, sir.

00:08:11.655 --> 00:08:14.818
Ensign Kim, I've been trying
to report a problem in the gym,

00:08:14.858 --> 00:08:16.758
but the com system
seems to be down.

00:08:16.794 --> 00:08:18.455
We've encountered
a spatial distortion.

00:08:18.495 --> 00:08:19.928
It's knocked out
several systems.

00:08:19.963 --> 00:08:22.363
Maybe that explains
why the gym got so cold.

00:08:22.399 --> 00:08:23.798
Cold?

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.062
Well, I didn't
notice it at first,

00:08:25.102 --> 00:08:26.126
I was working out so hard.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.933
Then I realized it was
under 10 degrees C.

00:08:28.005 --> 00:08:30.337
The environmental controls
didn't respond to my commands

00:08:30.374 --> 00:08:32.342
and neither did the com system.

00:08:32.376 --> 00:08:34.071
Engines are off-line, too.

00:08:34.111 --> 00:08:35.942
I'm looking for the Captain
to let her know what's going on.

00:08:36.046 --> 00:08:37.638
Should I report
to my duty station?

00:08:37.681 --> 00:08:38.943
Might not be a bad idea.

00:08:39.049 --> 00:08:41.040
Until we find out
exactly what's going on,

00:08:41.084 --> 00:08:42.608
everybody should be on standby.

00:08:42.653 --> 00:08:45.315
I'll round up
my security team.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.487
The first thing I want to do
when we get to the Bridge

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:54.360
is establish a remote com link
to Engineering.

00:08:54.398 --> 00:08:55.956
I want to know exactly
what's going on.

00:08:55.999 --> 00:08:58.467
Aye, Captain.

00:08:58.502 --> 00:08:59.560
Where are we?

00:08:59.603 --> 00:09:01.662
Deck 4.

00:09:01.705 --> 00:09:03.070
If the com system's
malfunctioning,

00:09:03.106 --> 00:09:05.574
the computer could be misreading
our voice commands.

00:09:05.609 --> 00:09:08.077
That might explain why it took
us here instead of the Bridge.

00:09:08.111 --> 00:09:10.739
We'd better try setting
the controls manually.

00:09:14.518 --> 00:09:17.248
Did you enjoy your first
surprise party, sweeting?

00:09:17.287 --> 00:09:18.914
It was wonderful.
Thank you.

00:09:18.956 --> 00:09:23.086
I thought you'd like it...
the cake, the presents.

00:09:23.126 --> 00:09:25.492
What was your favorite part?

00:09:25.529 --> 00:09:26.928
I suppose what I liked best

00:09:26.997 --> 00:09:28.897
was that all my friends
were there.

00:09:28.932 --> 00:09:30.593
Ah, that was nice, wasn't it?

00:09:30.634 --> 00:09:32.932
And don't forget
that beautiful necklace

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.438
Tom Paris gave you.

00:09:35.472 --> 00:09:36.939
Do you really like it?

00:09:36.974 --> 00:09:38.441
Oh, why wouldn't I like it?

00:09:38.475 --> 00:09:40.375
Paris obviously has
excellent taste.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.607
I was afraid you might be
a little jealous.

00:09:43.647 --> 00:09:44.875
Who, me?

00:09:44.915 --> 00:09:47.509
Oh, don't be silly.

00:09:47.551 --> 00:09:48.779
Are you sure?

00:09:48.819 --> 00:09:51.083
You, my dearest,
have seen the last

00:09:51.121 --> 00:09:53.954
of that green-eyed pus hog
called jealousy.

00:09:53.991 --> 00:09:55.891
I'm glad.

00:09:55.926 --> 00:09:59.953
Of course, Paris did
replicate that locket,

00:09:59.997 --> 00:10:04.297
whereas I baked the Jimbalian
fudge cake from scratch.

00:10:05.502 --> 00:10:07.800
These aren't my quarters.

00:10:07.838 --> 00:10:09.965
Did we take a wrong turn
somewhere?

00:10:10.007 --> 00:10:12.498
I was just following you.

00:10:24.087 --> 00:10:26.248
Is everything all right,
Lieutenant?

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.087
This isn't Engineering.

00:10:35.499 --> 00:10:36.466
And have someone take a look

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.491
at the turbolift voice
receptors, Commander.

00:10:38.535 --> 00:10:40.503
Aye, Captain.

00:10:40.537 --> 00:10:41.504
This is Engineering.

00:10:41.538 --> 00:10:42.664
What's going on here?

00:10:42.706 --> 00:10:43.764
Looks like we're dealing

00:10:43.807 --> 00:10:45.832
with more than just
a com system malfunction.

00:10:45.876 --> 00:10:48.037
Computer, Bridge.

00:11:18.742 --> 00:11:20.403
Baxter, what are you doing here?

00:11:20.444 --> 00:11:21.706
I wish I knew.

00:11:21.745 --> 00:11:23.645
I'm trying to get
to the cargo bay.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.841
And I'm trying to get
to Engineering.

00:11:25.882 --> 00:11:27.975
I can't find the cargo bay,

00:11:28.018 --> 00:11:29.485
and I can't find
my security team.

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:32.386
I've been wandering around
for about ten minutes.

00:11:32.422 --> 00:11:34.481
Well, at least
I know I'm not crazy...

00:11:34.524 --> 00:11:35.991
unless we both are.

00:11:36.026 --> 00:11:37.857
No. Something very strange
is going on.

00:11:37.894 --> 00:11:39.862
Ensign Kim said we had
encountered a spatial

00:11:39.896 --> 00:11:40.863
distortion.

00:11:40.897 --> 00:11:42.489
Did he say what kind?

00:11:42.532 --> 00:11:44.159
No, and he went to find
the Captain.

00:11:44.201 --> 00:11:46.692
The Captain is on her way
to the Bridge,

00:11:46.737 --> 00:11:48.329
but if she's having the
same trouble we are,

00:11:48.372 --> 00:11:50.670
- who knows if she can get there.
- Yeah.

00:11:51.875 --> 00:11:54.742
I'm going to keep trying
to get to Engineering.

00:11:54.778 --> 00:11:55.972
Good luck.

00:12:12.829 --> 00:12:14.126
The holodeck again.

00:12:14.164 --> 00:12:15.131
Aha!

00:12:15.165 --> 00:12:16.132
This is infuriating.

00:12:16.166 --> 00:12:19.294
Ah, stop playing games,
mon chéri.

00:12:19.336 --> 00:12:21.201
I know why you keep
coming back to work

00:12:21.238 --> 00:12:23.297
even though your
bartending shift is over.

00:12:24.341 --> 00:12:25.706
It's to see me, of course.

00:12:25.742 --> 00:12:27.471
How many times
do I have to tell you, madam?

00:12:27.511 --> 00:12:28.808
- Oh!
- I am a doctor, not a bartender.

00:12:28.845 --> 00:12:31.177
Of course, you are.

00:12:36.653 --> 00:12:37.813
Doc?

00:12:38.855 --> 00:12:39.981
Ensign Kim.

00:12:40.023 --> 00:12:41.320
I was just, uh...

00:12:41.358 --> 00:12:43.155
Playing doctor.

00:12:44.528 --> 00:12:46.052
Hi.

00:12:47.064 --> 00:12:48.190
Hi.

00:12:48.231 --> 00:12:50.461
The Captain and the others
went to investigate

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.230
the phenomenon
Mr. Tuvok reported.

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:55.830
So all of you heard his report
before the com system failed?

00:12:55.872 --> 00:12:57.169
Only a fraction of it.

00:12:57.207 --> 00:13:00.335
Well, I'm sure Tuvok's filled
them in with the rest by now.

00:13:00.377 --> 00:13:02.242
What are you still doing
on the holodeck, besides

00:13:02.279 --> 00:13:04.179
playing doctor, that is?

00:13:04.214 --> 00:13:06.614
For your information,
I have been attempting

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:08.618
to transfer myself
back to Sick Bay,

00:13:08.652 --> 00:13:11.553
but each time I try,
I reappear here.

00:13:11.588 --> 00:13:12.850
That's strange.

00:13:12.889 --> 00:13:14.481
Not to mention
extremely irritating.

00:13:14.524 --> 00:13:17.084
I can't seem to shut down
Mr. Paris'

00:13:17.127 --> 00:13:18.389
holo-program either.

00:13:18.428 --> 00:13:20.623
Computer, end holodeck
program Paris 3.

00:13:21.665 --> 00:13:22.632
Computer, arch.

00:13:24.868 --> 00:13:27.166
Either the holo-emitters
are malfunctioning,

00:13:27.204 --> 00:13:29.798
or the computer's not accepting
voice commands.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:30.966
I'm sorry, Doctor,

00:13:31.007 --> 00:13:32.304
I don't have time
to help you right now.

00:13:32.342 --> 00:13:33.809
- Wait just a minute.
- Hmm?

00:13:33.844 --> 00:13:35.243
Where do you think
you're going?

00:13:35.278 --> 00:13:36.336
I've got to get back
to the Bridge.

00:13:36.379 --> 00:13:37.539
We're in the middle of a crisis.

00:13:37.581 --> 00:13:39.708
All the more reason
I should be back in Sick Bay.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.342
I'm sure that the Captain
and the others

00:13:41.384 --> 00:13:43.579
will be able to do without you
for a few more minutes.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.781
I guess you're right.

00:13:45.822 --> 00:13:48.620
I'll have a look
at the holo-controls.

00:13:56.566 --> 00:13:59.364
Kyoto's quarters.

00:14:02.472 --> 00:14:03.905
Nicoletti.

00:14:05.041 --> 00:14:06.736
Hargrove.

00:14:08.545 --> 00:14:09.807
Ayala.

00:14:09.846 --> 00:14:12.576
None of those are
anywhere near my quarters.

00:14:12.616 --> 00:14:13.514
This is Deck 8.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:14.750
That's where your quarters are.

00:14:14.883 --> 00:14:17.613
But Hargrove and Ayala
are on Deck 7.

00:14:17.652 --> 00:14:18.949
Nicoletti is on 4,

00:14:18.987 --> 00:14:21.114
and I think Kyoto is on 6.

00:14:21.156 --> 00:14:24.387
How do you know
where everyone's quarters are?

00:14:24.426 --> 00:14:26.394
I just remember.

00:14:26.428 --> 00:14:28.794
Remember from what?

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.355
Have you been
in all their quarters?

00:14:31.399 --> 00:14:32.696
Of course not.

00:14:32.734 --> 00:14:35.202
The point is, those quarters
can't all be on the same deck.

00:14:35.237 --> 00:14:37.467
Well, see for yourself.

00:14:37.506 --> 00:14:40.441
This can't be.

00:14:40.475 --> 00:14:44.502
Perhaps, sweeting, your memory
isn't as reliable as you think.

00:14:44.546 --> 00:14:45.638
This is impossible.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.341
I know Hargrove is on 7.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.317
Why Hargrove?

00:14:50.352 --> 00:14:51.580
What?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.521
Why are you so sure
about Hargrove's quarters?

00:14:54.556 --> 00:14:57.286
What makes him... so special?

00:14:57.325 --> 00:14:58.724
He's not special.

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:01.558
I just remember
where his quarters are.

00:15:01.596 --> 00:15:02.927
This way.

00:15:02.998 --> 00:15:05.159
It has to be this way.

00:15:13.675 --> 00:15:14.869
Harry.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:18.073
B'Elanna, shouldn't you
be in Engineering?

00:15:18.113 --> 00:15:19.273
What are you doing here?

00:15:19.314 --> 00:15:21.441
Just answer one question,
Starfleet.

00:15:21.483 --> 00:15:22.609
Where is here?

00:15:22.651 --> 00:15:23.618
What?!

00:15:23.652 --> 00:15:24.949
Where am I?

00:15:24.986 --> 00:15:26.613
Outside Holodeck 2.

00:15:26.655 --> 00:15:28.452
Are you feeling okay?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.084
I have been walking in circles
for the past 20 minutes

00:15:31.126 --> 00:15:32.957
trying to get to Engineering.

00:15:32.994 --> 00:15:36.691
Kes, my sweet, you have many
wonderful attributes.

00:15:36.731 --> 00:15:39.757
Your sense of direction
is not one of them. I...

00:15:39.801 --> 00:15:42.793
Oh, uh, Harry, B'Elanna,
maybe you can help us.

00:15:42.838 --> 00:15:44.635
I know you'll find
this hard to believe,

00:15:44.673 --> 00:15:47.403
but we can't seem to find
Kes' quarters.

00:15:52.814 --> 00:15:53.906
I don't suppose

00:15:53.949 --> 00:15:56.349
anyone here knows
the way to the Bridge?

00:16:04.125 --> 00:16:05.422
Let me get this straight...

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:08.588
this distortion ring
has completely immobilized us.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.359
We have
no means of communication

00:16:10.398 --> 00:16:12.491
with the Bridge
or any other part of the ship,

00:16:12.534 --> 00:16:15.094
and no matter where any of us
have tried to go...

00:16:15.136 --> 00:16:17.536
the Bridge, Engineering,
Kes' quarters...

00:16:17.572 --> 00:16:20.097
we've all eventually
ended up here.

00:16:20.141 --> 00:16:22.701
Right back at Deck 6.

00:16:22.744 --> 00:16:26.111
The Bridge is on Deck 1.
Engineering is on Deck 11.

00:16:26.147 --> 00:16:28.707
Deck 6 is halfway
in between, right?

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.876
So?

00:16:29.918 --> 00:16:32.546
So, if we're being surrounded
by this ring,

00:16:32.587 --> 00:16:34.578
maybe it's pushing us all
to the center of the ship.

00:16:34.623 --> 00:16:37.057
But it's not just that
we're being led back here.

00:16:37.092 --> 00:16:38.957
I mean, rooms are
in the wrong place.

00:16:38.994 --> 00:16:41.462
Is it possible
that this distortion ring

00:16:41.496 --> 00:16:45.296
is somehow changing
the layout of the ship?

00:16:45.333 --> 00:16:47.301
There is another possibility.

00:16:47.335 --> 00:16:49.303
Exposure to some types
of EM radiation

00:16:49.337 --> 00:16:52.135
has been known to cause
hallucinations.

00:16:52.173 --> 00:16:54.733
Perhaps it's not the ship
that's undergone changes

00:16:54.776 --> 00:16:56.971
but rather
your perception of it.

00:16:57.012 --> 00:16:58.980
Unfortunately,
without my medical equipment

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.605
to analyze your optic nerves,
there's no way to tell.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.447
We'll never figure it out
sitting here.

00:17:03.485 --> 00:17:05.749
We need more information
about this phenomenon...

00:17:05.787 --> 00:17:07.914
sensor readings,
computer analyses.

00:17:07.956 --> 00:17:11.016
We have to find a way
back to the Bridge.

00:17:11.059 --> 00:17:13.254
If we can't get back on foot
or on the turbolift,

00:17:13.295 --> 00:17:15.195
maybe we can rig
a site-to-site transport...

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:17.630
beam ourselves to the Bridge.

00:17:17.666 --> 00:17:19.827
We'd have to get
to a transporter room first.

00:17:19.868 --> 00:17:21.165
Or to Engineering.

00:17:21.202 --> 00:17:23.500
Wherever that is.

00:17:23.538 --> 00:17:25.768
When we tried to go
to the Bridge,

00:17:25.807 --> 00:17:28.799
one of the places the turbolift
took us was Engineering.

00:17:28.843 --> 00:17:31.403
Maybe if we repeat our steps,
it'll take us back there.

00:17:31.446 --> 00:17:32.413
It's worth a shot.

00:17:32.447 --> 00:17:36.440
Lieutenant Paris,
you're with Torres.

00:17:37.686 --> 00:17:40.177
Maybe we can get to the Bridge
through a Jefferies tube.

00:17:40.221 --> 00:17:41.848
If I remember my ship specs
correctly,

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.824
there should be
an emergency access conduit

00:17:43.858 --> 00:17:45.416
which leads directly
from this deck

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.690
to Deck 1,
right behind the Bridge.

00:17:47.729 --> 00:17:49.959
I'd like to keep trying
to get to the Bridge on foot.

00:17:49.998 --> 00:17:52.899
If the ship has been
reconfigured somehow, I can get

00:17:52.934 --> 00:17:55.368
a deck-by-deck picture
of what it looks like as I go.

00:17:55.403 --> 00:17:57.064
What's going to keep you
from getting lost?

00:17:57.105 --> 00:17:59.300
I'll get a tricorder
from the storage locker,

00:17:59.341 --> 00:18:00.740
rig it to emit
a photoplasmic trail.

00:18:00.775 --> 00:18:01.742
Right.

00:18:01.776 --> 00:18:03.368
We should all get tricorders.

00:18:03.411 --> 00:18:04.571
Set them on active scan,

00:18:04.612 --> 00:18:06.045
gather as much information
as we can

00:18:06.081 --> 00:18:07.514
about what's happening
to the ship.

00:18:07.549 --> 00:18:08.538
May I request that Kes

00:18:08.583 --> 00:18:10.278
be allowed to stay
here with me?

00:18:10.318 --> 00:18:12.343
Besides helping stave off

00:18:12.387 --> 00:18:15.845
the predatory advances
of that... woman,

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:17.881
she may be able
to help me find a way

00:18:17.926 --> 00:18:19.917
to transfer myself
back to Sick Bay.

00:18:19.995 --> 00:18:24.591
And, uh, I'll assist
Commander Chakotay, Captain.

00:18:24.632 --> 00:18:25.929
As you may have heard,

00:18:25.967 --> 00:18:29.630
my tracking skills are legendary
throughout the quadrant.

00:18:29.671 --> 00:18:31.730
That all right with you,
Commander?

00:18:33.641 --> 00:18:35.905
Mr. Kim, I'm with you.

00:18:35.944 --> 00:18:36.933
Let's do it.

00:18:39.647 --> 00:18:41.114
Be careful.

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:44.778
Are you sure this is
how you got there before?

00:18:44.819 --> 00:18:46.946
Relax, will you?

00:18:46.988 --> 00:18:49.786
So far, we're right on schedule.

00:18:49.824 --> 00:18:51.348
The next stop should be...

00:18:53.495 --> 00:18:55.156
...Voila. Engineering.

00:18:55.196 --> 00:18:57.130
Finally.
Let's get to work.

00:18:57.165 --> 00:18:59.395
We've got an emergency situation
on board ship.

00:18:59.434 --> 00:19:01.197
I don't have time
to go into details,

00:19:01.236 --> 00:19:03.067
but you're all to remain
at your posts

00:19:03.104 --> 00:19:04.230
until otherwise notified,

00:19:04.272 --> 00:19:06.240
whether or not
your duty shifts are over.

00:19:06.274 --> 00:19:08.742
Ensign, prepare to configure
transporter systems

00:19:08.777 --> 00:19:10.074
for a site-to-site transport.

00:19:10.111 --> 00:19:12.079
I've got to reset
the pattern buffer controls.

00:19:12.113 --> 00:19:13.080
In the meantime,

00:19:13.114 --> 00:19:15.378
why don't you check
the targeting scanners?

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:21.345
Crewman...

00:19:21.389 --> 00:19:24.586
there's a-an emergency situation
aboard ship.

00:19:24.626 --> 00:19:27.060
Just...
stay right where you are.

00:19:27.095 --> 00:19:28.892
That's an order.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:40.464
I think you handled that
very well, Lieutenant.

00:19:51.152 --> 00:19:54.781
Commander, I would imagine

00:19:54.823 --> 00:19:57.792
you've had
some experience with women.

00:19:58.993 --> 00:20:00.290
Some.

00:20:00.328 --> 00:20:02.455
Oh, come now! Ha!

00:20:02.497 --> 00:20:06.627
A... a... a
handsome man like you.

00:20:06.668 --> 00:20:08.295
I bet women find
you irresistible.

00:20:10.338 --> 00:20:13.739
Neelix, what's this about?

00:20:13.775 --> 00:20:14.901
Uh...

00:20:14.943 --> 00:20:17.503
um... uh...

00:20:17.545 --> 00:20:20.309
have you... uh...

00:20:20.348 --> 00:20:23.875
have you... ever been jealous?

00:20:25.854 --> 00:20:27.344
Of course.

00:20:27.388 --> 00:20:28.980
You have?

00:20:29.057 --> 00:20:31.992
I imagine most people
who have been in love

00:20:32.026 --> 00:20:33.516
have been jealous
at one time or another.

00:20:33.561 --> 00:20:35.825
I see!

00:20:35.864 --> 00:20:38.992
L-lt's a perfectly
normal response.

00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:43.026
Then why...
why is it so unpleasant?

00:20:45.206 --> 00:20:48.471
Jealousy's about the fear
of losing someone we love.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.308
There's no pain
greater than that.

00:20:54.883 --> 00:20:57.511
Neelix...

00:20:57.552 --> 00:21:00.680
are you afraid you're going
to lose Kes to someone?

00:21:00.722 --> 00:21:02.121
No.

00:21:02.157 --> 00:21:05.126
I mean, I-I-I don't think so.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.129
At least, I certainly hope not.

00:21:08.163 --> 00:21:10.290
I-I... I just
can't seem to stop

00:21:10.331 --> 00:21:12.629
these awful feelings.

00:21:12.667 --> 00:21:16.967
Nothing makes us more vulnerable
than when we love someone.

00:21:17.005 --> 00:21:19.633
We can be hurt very easily.

00:21:19.674 --> 00:21:21.301
But I've always believed

00:21:21.342 --> 00:21:23.310
that what you get
when you love someone

00:21:23.344 --> 00:21:25.278
is greater than what you risk.

00:21:25.313 --> 00:21:27.304
Commander,
am I ever glad to see you.

00:21:27.348 --> 00:21:28.645
Do you have any idea
what's going on?

00:21:28.683 --> 00:21:29.877
Not exactly.

00:21:29.918 --> 00:21:31.783
Well, I feel like I've been
wandering around for hours.

00:21:31.819 --> 00:21:33.150
I can't find the cargo bay.

00:21:33.188 --> 00:21:35.281
Have you seen anyone else?
Any more of the crew?

00:21:35.323 --> 00:21:37.814
Some people roaming around
like me.

00:21:37.859 --> 00:21:39.588
A couple of times
I wound up in the Mess Hall.

00:21:39.627 --> 00:21:41.094
There were quite
a few people there.

00:21:41.129 --> 00:21:42.460
I suggest
you make your way back.

00:21:42.497 --> 00:21:44.294
Tell everyone you run into
to come with you,

00:21:44.332 --> 00:21:45.993
and all of you stay put
in the Mess Hall.

00:21:46.067 --> 00:21:46.999
When we figure out

00:21:47.068 --> 00:21:49.263
what's going on,
we'll let you know.

00:21:49.304 --> 00:21:50.635
Aye, Commander.

00:21:58.046 --> 00:21:59.707
Gentlemen.

00:22:01.149 --> 00:22:02.446
Tuvok,
what are you doing here?

00:22:02.483 --> 00:22:04.144
That is an interesting
question, Commander.

00:22:04.185 --> 00:22:06.949
I am not certain
how I arrived at this location.

00:22:06.988 --> 00:22:08.285
You're lost, too.

00:22:08.323 --> 00:22:09.620
Indeed.

00:22:09.657 --> 00:22:11.625
When I received no word
from you or the Captain,

00:22:11.659 --> 00:22:13.684
I left Lieutenant Ayala
in command

00:22:13.728 --> 00:22:15.696
and came to look for you myself.

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.163
Can you lead us back
to the Bridge?

00:22:17.198 --> 00:22:19.291
I do not believe so.

00:22:19.334 --> 00:22:21.302
When I first realized
I was lost,

00:22:21.336 --> 00:22:23.304
I attempted to retrace my steps,

00:22:23.338 --> 00:22:24.828
only to find myself here.

00:22:24.872 --> 00:22:27.238
None of us has been able
to reach the Bridge.

00:22:27.275 --> 00:22:29.641
In fact, Neelix and I
can't seem to get off Deck 6.

00:22:29.677 --> 00:22:33.135
Strange.
I thought we were on Deck 3.

00:22:36.017 --> 00:22:38.485
What was our status
when you left the Bridge?

00:22:38.519 --> 00:22:39.986
The ring has penetrated
our shields

00:22:40.021 --> 00:22:42.819
and is now in direct contact
with the hull.

00:22:42.857 --> 00:22:44.757
Then maybe it is possible
the distortions

00:22:44.792 --> 00:22:46.453
are somehow
reconfiguring the ship.

00:22:46.494 --> 00:22:48.086
As improbable as it sounds,

00:22:48.129 --> 00:22:50.131
that would appear
to be the case.

00:22:50.264 --> 00:22:52.061
Neelix, let's go.

00:22:55.035 --> 00:22:56.696
Neelix.

00:23:10.918 --> 00:23:12.943
I don't understand it.

00:23:12.987 --> 00:23:16.150
We should have found the hatch
to the Bridge ten minutes ago.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:17.782
I feel like
we're crawling in circles.

00:23:17.825 --> 00:23:18.792
But we haven't...

00:23:18.826 --> 00:23:20.453
at least not according
to this tricorder.

00:23:21.629 --> 00:23:22.596
Odd!

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:23.824
What is it?

00:23:23.864 --> 00:23:26.059
A very faint
electromagnetic reading.

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:29.297
Now it's gone.

00:23:29.336 --> 00:23:31.304
There it is
from another direction.

00:23:31.338 --> 00:23:32.464
Yeah, I'm getting it, too.

00:23:32.506 --> 00:23:33.632
It comes and goes.

00:23:33.674 --> 00:23:35.835
Jumps from place to place.

00:23:35.876 --> 00:23:38.174
Could it be evidence
of the ship's reconfiguration?

00:23:38.212 --> 00:23:39.440
Possibly.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:43.814
We'll have to compare this data
with readings the others get.

00:23:43.851 --> 00:23:45.148
Harry?

00:23:45.186 --> 00:23:46.983
Yes, ma'am?

00:23:47.021 --> 00:23:49.148
I just want you to know...

00:23:49.190 --> 00:23:51.158
you've been one
of the bright spots

00:23:51.192 --> 00:23:52.250
of this whole mission.

00:23:52.293 --> 00:23:55.091
You've exceeded any expectations
I might have had of you.

00:23:55.129 --> 00:23:57.996
Thank you, Captain.

00:23:58.032 --> 00:24:01.433
I... I appreciate that.

00:24:04.872 --> 00:24:06.032
Wait a minute.

00:24:07.174 --> 00:24:08.436
Down there.

00:24:08.475 --> 00:24:10.534
I think that's the conduit
leading to the Bridge.

00:24:10.578 --> 00:24:11.772
Good work.

00:24:11.812 --> 00:24:15.339
Maybe now we'll get
some answers.

00:24:15.382 --> 00:24:16.508
That's the hatch, Captain.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:18.279
This should let us out
in the cargo hold

00:24:18.319 --> 00:24:21.117
directly behind the Bridge.

00:24:21.155 --> 00:24:22.952
It's not working.

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:25.083
We'd better try it manually.

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:35.366
It's stuck.

00:24:35.402 --> 00:24:36.562
Oh!

00:24:37.771 --> 00:24:38.738
Oh...

00:24:38.772 --> 00:24:39.898
Captain!

00:24:50.084 --> 00:24:52.518
I... c-can't...

00:24:52.553 --> 00:24:55.920
get my arm out.

00:24:55.956 --> 00:24:59.414
Oh! Oh...

00:25:01.962 --> 00:25:03.930
Oh...

00:25:10.371 --> 00:25:12.965
I think I'm okay.

00:25:15.976 --> 00:25:18.103
I'm reading an intense
electromagnetic charge

00:25:18.145 --> 00:25:19.442
on the other side of that hatch.

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:21.311
That must have been
what was pulling you in.

00:25:21.348 --> 00:25:23.782
It's as if everything
on the other side

00:25:23.817 --> 00:25:26.479
is in a state
of structural flux...

00:25:26.520 --> 00:25:28.283
the walls, the atmosphere...

00:25:28.322 --> 00:25:30.620
And the sequence
of those fluctuations

00:25:30.658 --> 00:25:32.683
matches the readings
from the distortion ring.

00:25:32.726 --> 00:25:35.160
This phenomenon isn't just
occurring in space.

00:25:35.195 --> 00:25:37.390
It's definitely inside the ship
as well.

00:25:37.431 --> 00:25:38.898
We're going to have to regroup

00:25:38.932 --> 00:25:41.298
and come up with a plan
for combating this thing.

00:25:43.237 --> 00:25:44.727
Captain, what's wrong?

00:25:44.772 --> 00:25:46.967
I don't know.

00:25:47.007 --> 00:25:48.634
Oh...

00:25:48.676 --> 00:25:50.576
Oh, my eyes...

00:25:50.611 --> 00:25:51.703
Captain?

00:25:51.745 --> 00:25:53.042
Captain!

00:25:54.815 --> 00:25:58.148
Come on, pal, one lousy game.

00:25:58.185 --> 00:25:59.812
I'll spot you six balls.

00:25:59.853 --> 00:26:01.753
I'm not programmed
to play games.

00:26:01.789 --> 00:26:03.416
If he won't play pool with you,

00:26:03.457 --> 00:26:04.583
and he won't make love to me,

00:26:04.625 --> 00:26:08.254
then as far as I'm concerned,
he can mop the floor.

00:26:08.295 --> 00:26:09.762
You see these hands?

00:26:09.797 --> 00:26:11.094
These are surgeon's hands,

00:26:11.131 --> 00:26:12.257
created
by the most sophisticated

00:26:12.299 --> 00:26:14.267
computer imaging technology
available.

00:26:14.301 --> 00:26:17.759
They do not play games,
and they do not mop floors!

00:26:17.805 --> 00:26:19.272
Then you are fired.

00:26:19.306 --> 00:26:20.432
I will find a new bartender.

00:26:20.474 --> 00:26:23.568
I really wish you would.

00:26:23.610 --> 00:26:25.134
Doctor...

00:26:25.179 --> 00:26:26.771
Please tell me
you've had some success

00:26:26.814 --> 00:26:28.213
in reinitializing
the holo-emitters.

00:26:28.248 --> 00:26:29.442
I did exactly what you told me,

00:26:29.483 --> 00:26:30.450
but it didn't work.

00:26:30.484 --> 00:26:31.781
Of course not.

00:26:31.819 --> 00:26:33.286
I'm starting to get worried
about Neelix.

00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:34.287
What's taking them so long?

00:26:34.321 --> 00:26:35.447
Ah, trust me, chérie.

00:26:35.489 --> 00:26:36.615
You are better off without him.

00:26:36.657 --> 00:26:38.625
All men are alike.

00:26:38.659 --> 00:26:41.628
In the end,
they always break your heart.

00:26:41.662 --> 00:26:43.960
Can I get some help here?

00:26:43.997 --> 00:26:45.225
What happened to her?

00:26:45.265 --> 00:26:47.130
She came into contact
with the spatial distortions

00:26:47.167 --> 00:26:48.293
in the Jefferies tube.

00:26:48.335 --> 00:26:49.700
She seemed fine
for a couple minutes,

00:26:49.737 --> 00:26:51.932
but then she started to fade
in and out of consciousness.

00:26:59.113 --> 00:27:02.913
I believe we should
go this way, Commander.

00:27:02.950 --> 00:27:04.577
Wh-What makes you say that?

00:27:04.618 --> 00:27:07.246
If we are indeed trapped
in some sort of labyrinth,

00:27:07.287 --> 00:27:09.653
then the logical course is
to systematically eliminate

00:27:09.690 --> 00:27:12.318
all routes which do not lead us
to our desired destination.

00:27:12.359 --> 00:27:16.159
The route that remains
will be the correct one.

00:27:16.196 --> 00:27:17.925
Since we have been making
a series of right turns,

00:27:17.965 --> 00:27:20.832
we should continue to do so
until we are certain

00:27:20.868 --> 00:27:22.768
this path is not the proper one.

00:27:22.803 --> 00:27:24.634
There's a flaw in your logic.

00:27:24.671 --> 00:27:26.866
How so, Commander?

00:27:26.907 --> 00:27:28.431
You're assuming
there's a logical pattern

00:27:28.475 --> 00:27:29.567
to this maze we're caught in,

00:27:29.610 --> 00:27:31.407
but so far I haven't seen
any evidence of that.

00:27:31.445 --> 00:27:34.209
Even within chaotic systems,

00:27:34.248 --> 00:27:36.409
there is a pattern
of limited predictability.

00:27:36.450 --> 00:27:38.042
By the time we figure
that pattern out,

00:27:38.085 --> 00:27:40.451
these distortions may have
completely overrun the ship.

00:27:40.487 --> 00:27:42.955
That is a possibility.

00:27:42.990 --> 00:27:44.651
The important thing is
for at least one of us

00:27:44.691 --> 00:27:45.851
to make it back to the Bridge.

00:27:45.893 --> 00:27:47.656
So why don't you go your way,
and I'll go mine.

00:27:47.694 --> 00:27:49.628
That way, we'll increase
the chances that one of us

00:27:49.663 --> 00:27:51.290
will be successful.

00:27:51.331 --> 00:27:53.060
As you wish, Commander.

00:28:07.614 --> 00:28:09.241
Tell me something, Tuvok.

00:28:09.283 --> 00:28:11.911
What does your logic tell you
about navigating a maze

00:28:11.985 --> 00:28:13.680
that's constantly
changing shape?

00:28:17.758 --> 00:28:18.850
Scanners check out.

00:28:18.892 --> 00:28:20.587
Then we're ready
to give it a try.

00:28:20.627 --> 00:28:22.492
Activate the auxiliary
pattern buffers.

00:28:22.529 --> 00:28:23.757
Pattern buffers activated.

00:28:23.797 --> 00:28:26.095
Targeting the Bridge
coordinates.

00:28:26.133 --> 00:28:28.465
Scanners locked.

00:28:31.605 --> 00:28:33.596
Energize.

00:28:47.521 --> 00:28:50.490
Would you mind moving
your foot, Tommy boy?

00:28:50.524 --> 00:28:52.617
It's blocking my shot.

00:28:56.497 --> 00:28:58.055
Tell me you already
made it to the Bridge,

00:28:58.098 --> 00:29:00.123
and you've come back here
to give us a status report.

00:29:00.167 --> 00:29:01.566
We locked on
to the Bridge coordinates,

00:29:01.602 --> 00:29:04.070
but this is where we ended up.

00:29:04.104 --> 00:29:05.332
None of you had any luck either?

00:29:05.372 --> 00:29:07.397
Not only has no one been able
to reach the Bridge,

00:29:07.441 --> 00:29:09.409
but the Captain
came into contact

00:29:09.443 --> 00:29:11.877
with the spatial distortion
and is now unconscious.

00:29:11.912 --> 00:29:13.174
That's not all.

00:29:13.213 --> 00:29:14.237
We lost Neelix, too.

00:29:14.281 --> 00:29:15.908
Lost him?

00:29:15.949 --> 00:29:18.747
He turned a corner,
and he was just gone.

00:29:18.785 --> 00:29:21.754
We think the spatial distortions
are continuously changing

00:29:21.788 --> 00:29:23.483
the configuration
of the corridors.

00:29:23.524 --> 00:29:25.082
Kes must be worried sick.

00:29:25.125 --> 00:29:28.424
And it isn't just Neelix
who's missing.

00:29:28.462 --> 00:29:29.759
Where's the rest of the crew?

00:29:29.796 --> 00:29:31.093
It is likely that they, too,

00:29:31.131 --> 00:29:32.928
are trapped
in other parts of the ship,

00:29:32.966 --> 00:29:36.026
cut off from communication and
unable to find their way out.

00:29:36.069 --> 00:29:37.263
So, what do we do now?

00:29:37.304 --> 00:29:39.704
This wave is obviously causing

00:29:39.740 --> 00:29:41.901
some kind of radical
reconfiguration of the ship.

00:29:41.942 --> 00:29:43.341
We've got to try to reverse it.

00:29:43.377 --> 00:29:46.107
If not, we may never be
able to get to the Bridge.

00:29:46.146 --> 00:29:49.604
How are we supposed to reverse
something we don't understand?

00:29:49.650 --> 00:29:51.515
No matter where we go,
we end up here.

00:29:51.552 --> 00:29:54.953
Corridors are realigning,
rooms are in the wrong place...

00:29:55.055 --> 00:29:55.953
What's the pattern?

00:29:56.056 --> 00:29:58.286
We would certainly
benefit from having

00:29:58.325 --> 00:30:00.623
an accurate picture of what
the ship currently looks like.

00:30:00.661 --> 00:30:02.185
That way we would have
a better chance

00:30:02.229 --> 00:30:04.129
of getting where we want to go.

00:30:04.164 --> 00:30:06.132
Maybe we could make a map.

00:30:06.166 --> 00:30:07.133
Ensign?

00:30:07.167 --> 00:30:08.634
One good thing

00:30:08.669 --> 00:30:10.102
about all the wandering
we've been doing

00:30:10.137 --> 00:30:12.071
is that we've been collecting
a lot of tricorder data

00:30:12.105 --> 00:30:14.130
about the structural changes
that have been taking place.

00:30:14.174 --> 00:30:15.801
And if we fed
all that information

00:30:15.842 --> 00:30:18.436
into the central database,
the computer might be able

00:30:18.478 --> 00:30:21.538
to extrapolate a schematic of
the ship as it's configured now.

00:30:21.582 --> 00:30:23.573
What are we waiting for?

00:30:29.022 --> 00:30:31.991
The computer has analyzed
all our tricorder data,

00:30:32.025 --> 00:30:34.721
so this ought to be pretty close
to what it looks like now.

00:30:36.530 --> 00:30:39.727
It's as if the entire ship
is being compressed

00:30:39.766 --> 00:30:40.960
and twisted.

00:30:41.001 --> 00:30:44.437
My guess is, it's more
than just a distortion ring.

00:30:44.471 --> 00:30:47.463
It looks like some sort
of spatial implosion

00:30:47.507 --> 00:30:49.407
that's slowly crushing us.

00:30:51.709 --> 00:30:55.008
Look... this part of the ship
seems unaffected.

00:30:55.045 --> 00:30:56.478
That's Deck 6, where we are.

00:30:56.514 --> 00:30:57.503
Correct, Ensign.

00:30:57.548 --> 00:30:59.379
However, the area
we are occupying

00:30:59.417 --> 00:31:01.612
will not remain
unaffected indefinitely.

00:31:01.652 --> 00:31:03.643
How long?

00:31:03.687 --> 00:31:06.281
Based on the rate
of implosion thus far,

00:31:06.323 --> 00:31:08.086
I estimate the ring
will crush Deck 6

00:31:08.125 --> 00:31:10.992
in approximately 68 minutes.

00:31:23.174 --> 00:31:25.972
Is this implosion ring
some kind of weapon?

00:31:26.010 --> 00:31:27.477
Are we under attack?

00:31:27.511 --> 00:31:29.138
Who'd want to attack us and why?

00:31:29.180 --> 00:31:30.670
There is no clear evidence

00:31:30.714 --> 00:31:32.978
of an intelligence
behind the phenomenon.

00:31:33.017 --> 00:31:34.143
It is still possible

00:31:34.185 --> 00:31:36.449
we are dealing with
a naturally occurring anomaly

00:31:36.487 --> 00:31:38.955
which does not conform
to the known laws of physics.

00:31:38.989 --> 00:31:41.355
Don't you think it's a little
late to be speculating on who

00:31:41.392 --> 00:31:42.950
or what this thing is?

00:31:42.993 --> 00:31:44.927
The important thing now
is that we find out some way

00:31:44.962 --> 00:31:45.929
of stopping it.

00:31:45.963 --> 00:31:46.861
B'Elanna's right.

00:31:46.897 --> 00:31:49.331
It seems to me
we've got two options:

00:31:49.366 --> 00:31:50.993
One, we find a way
to get ourselves out

00:31:51.035 --> 00:31:52.366
of this implosion ring,
or two,

00:31:52.403 --> 00:31:54.598
we find some way
of reversing it.

00:31:54.638 --> 00:31:55.605
Invert the effect.

00:31:55.639 --> 00:31:57.106
Turn the implosion
into an explosion.

00:31:57.141 --> 00:31:58.267
Exactly.

00:31:58.309 --> 00:31:59.503
If I can get back
to Engineering,

00:31:59.543 --> 00:32:00.510
I may be able to generate

00:32:00.544 --> 00:32:02.136
a shock pulse strong enough
to do just that.

00:32:02.179 --> 00:32:03.646
Of course I'd have
to raise the pressure

00:32:03.681 --> 00:32:04.943
in the warp core
to near-critical.

00:32:04.982 --> 00:32:07.212
A shock pulse of that magnitude
would create

00:32:07.251 --> 00:32:09.617
a subatomic particle shower
all over the ship.

00:32:09.653 --> 00:32:10.950
Which could set off

00:32:11.021 --> 00:32:12.318
a chain reaction
that would cause

00:32:12.356 --> 00:32:13.789
not only the ring
to explode outward

00:32:13.824 --> 00:32:15.314
but Voyager along with it.

00:32:15.359 --> 00:32:18.123
Not if I can precisely tune
the shock pulse

00:32:18.162 --> 00:32:20.187
to the distortion frequency
of the ring.

00:32:20.231 --> 00:32:22.131
That will be
exceptionally difficult.

00:32:22.166 --> 00:32:23.428
If we don't give this a try,

00:32:23.467 --> 00:32:24.957
we're going
to get crushed anyway.

00:32:25.002 --> 00:32:28.301
Personally, I'd rather
go down fighting.

00:32:28.339 --> 00:32:30.364
I must remind you
that with the com system down,

00:32:30.407 --> 00:32:33.137
we will have no effective means
of alerting the rest of the crew

00:32:33.177 --> 00:32:34.872
to a potentially lethal
particle shower.

00:32:34.912 --> 00:32:37.244
Do you have another suggestion,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:32:37.281 --> 00:32:38.908
I believe it would be safer

00:32:38.949 --> 00:32:41.509
to attempt to access
the navigational array

00:32:41.552 --> 00:32:45.079
and from there engage thrusters
to steer us out of the ring.

00:32:45.122 --> 00:32:47.283
Can't we try both?

00:32:47.324 --> 00:32:49.417
It's much too dangerous
to have someone working

00:32:49.460 --> 00:32:51.360
at the navigational array
during a shock pulse.

00:32:51.395 --> 00:32:53.226
Besides,
this ship is so contorted,

00:32:53.264 --> 00:32:56.665
there's no reason to expect we'd
have any navigational control.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:59.328
All right, B'Elanna, let's give
your plan a shot. You...

00:32:59.370 --> 00:33:00.496
Commander Chakotay.

00:33:00.538 --> 00:33:01.698
Yes, Lieutenant?

00:33:01.739 --> 00:33:02.933
I feel compelled to point out

00:33:03.007 --> 00:33:04.440
that in my many years
of experience

00:33:04.475 --> 00:33:06.136
as Captain Janeway's
technical officer,

00:33:06.176 --> 00:33:09.270
she often demonstrated
a tendency to follow...

00:33:09.313 --> 00:33:10.439
In case you hadn't noticed,

00:33:10.481 --> 00:33:11.709
Captain Janeway's
not in any condition

00:33:11.749 --> 00:33:13.046
to make decisions.

00:33:13.083 --> 00:33:14.243
I'm in command.

00:33:14.285 --> 00:33:15.582
Is that understood?

00:33:15.619 --> 00:33:17.416
Yes, sir.

00:33:17.454 --> 00:33:18.751
Good.

00:33:18.789 --> 00:33:21.280
B'Elanna, you and Harry
get down to Engineering.

00:33:21.325 --> 00:33:22.952
Evacuate whoever's on duty.

00:33:22.993 --> 00:33:24.722
Then initiate the warp pulse.

00:33:24.762 --> 00:33:26.992
Move it.

00:33:33.771 --> 00:33:35.136
Dilithium matrix stable.

00:33:35.172 --> 00:33:37.970
Matter/antimatter reactor
is at 80 percent of critical.

00:33:38.008 --> 00:33:39.168
Let's keep it that way!

00:33:39.209 --> 00:33:41.336
Warp core pressure is at
36 megapascals and rising.

00:33:41.378 --> 00:33:44.108
When it reaches 53,
it'll trigger the shock pulse.

00:33:44.148 --> 00:33:46.844
We should get out of here
by the time it hits 50!

00:33:46.884 --> 00:33:47.976
Acknowledged.

00:33:48.052 --> 00:33:49.610
Pressure at 41 megapascals
and rising.

00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:51.883
I'm reading a micro-fracture
in the dilithium matrix.

00:33:51.922 --> 00:33:53.753
Attempting to compensate.

00:33:53.791 --> 00:33:55.418
Fracture sealed.

00:33:55.459 --> 00:33:56.858
44 megapascals!

00:34:00.197 --> 00:34:01.459
They're heating up
the warp core.

00:34:01.498 --> 00:34:03.466
They must be close
to initiating the shock burst.

00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:04.899
Everybody, take cover.

00:34:07.137 --> 00:34:10.197
47, 48, 49!

00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:11.730
Let's move!

00:34:24.655 --> 00:34:28.147
Well, in spite
of Tuvok's dire predictions,

00:34:28.192 --> 00:34:30.285
we haven't blown the ship
to pieces, have we?

00:34:30.327 --> 00:34:32.557
No, and radiation levels are
within acceptable tolerance.

00:34:32.596 --> 00:34:34.621
Good. Let's get in there
and see if we had any luck

00:34:34.665 --> 00:34:36.792
dispersing
this implosion ring.

00:34:37.835 --> 00:34:39.462
- Hold it.
- What?

00:34:39.503 --> 00:34:41.494
I'm reading a massive distortion
behind the door.

00:34:42.473 --> 00:34:45.465
I don't think
it's just behind the door.

00:34:45.509 --> 00:34:48.137
The ring's completely
engulfed Engineering.

00:34:54.685 --> 00:34:55.982
Can I talk to her?

00:34:56.020 --> 00:34:58.250
I can't guarantee
she'll hear you

00:34:58.288 --> 00:35:00.256
or be able to understand you
if she does.

00:35:03.093 --> 00:35:04.219
Captain.

00:35:07.464 --> 00:35:13.096
Talk... can't.

00:35:13.137 --> 00:35:14.468
What's wrong with her?

00:35:14.505 --> 00:35:16.439
It's possible
the spatial distortions

00:35:16.473 --> 00:35:18.134
have damaged her speech center.

00:35:18.175 --> 00:35:22.271
But without my equipment,
I can't analyze...

00:35:22.312 --> 00:35:24.803
...her neural pathways.

00:35:24.848 --> 00:35:27.612
Chakotay, it didn't work.

00:35:27.651 --> 00:35:29.482
Instead of forcing
the implosion outward,

00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:32.250
the pulse is drawing it in
at a faster rate.

00:35:32.289 --> 00:35:33.620
You're saying
it made things worse?

00:35:33.657 --> 00:35:35.454
I don't think we have
more than a few minutes.

00:35:35.492 --> 00:35:37.722
Paris, we have to get
to the navigational array

00:35:37.761 --> 00:35:39.126
and give Tuvok's plan a try.

00:35:39.163 --> 00:35:41.631
I'm afraid there's
no longer time for that.

00:35:41.665 --> 00:35:43.257
Why not?

00:35:49.139 --> 00:35:52.040
We're not going anywhere.

00:36:10.594 --> 00:36:12.687
Do you really think
it's possible to project

00:36:12.730 --> 00:36:14.357
a stable holographic
force field?

00:36:14.398 --> 00:36:16.093
We've tried everything else.

00:36:16.133 --> 00:36:17.225
Ready?

00:36:17.267 --> 00:36:20.134
Here we go.

00:36:27.478 --> 00:36:30.447
The distortion is unaffected
by the force field.

00:36:30.481 --> 00:36:33.177
We've got to figure out a way
to generate a stable field.

00:36:33.217 --> 00:36:34.343
B'Elanna,

00:36:34.384 --> 00:36:35.408
this ring has passed
through the shields,

00:36:35.452 --> 00:36:37.249
crushed the hull,
twisted the ship.

00:36:37.287 --> 00:36:38.777
We'll never get enough power

00:36:38.822 --> 00:36:40.619
from the holo-emitters
to stop it.

00:36:40.657 --> 00:36:43.091
What are you saying,
we're out of options?

00:36:43.127 --> 00:36:44.321
Perhaps not.

00:36:44.361 --> 00:36:47.194
So far we have been unsuccessful
in all our attempts

00:36:47.231 --> 00:36:49.631
to either explain or combat
this phenomenon,

00:36:49.666 --> 00:36:51.463
and according
to my calculations,

00:36:51.502 --> 00:36:53.129
the space
we are currently occupying

00:36:53.170 --> 00:36:56.435
will implode in approximately
three minutes, 17 seconds.

00:36:56.473 --> 00:36:58.202
You said there was
another option.

00:36:58.242 --> 00:37:00.335
We do nothing.

00:37:00.377 --> 00:37:02.402
Excuse me?

00:37:02.446 --> 00:37:04.676
Are you suggesting
we just let it crush us?

00:37:04.715 --> 00:37:06.114
Precisely.

00:37:07.151 --> 00:37:08.743
I can't believe
I'm hearing this from you.

00:37:08.786 --> 00:37:10.811
I agree... it sounds
completely illogical.

00:37:10.854 --> 00:37:12.082
On the contrary.

00:37:12.122 --> 00:37:14.852
When every logical
course of action is exhausted,

00:37:14.892 --> 00:37:16.917
the option that remains
is inaction.

00:37:16.960 --> 00:37:18.222
So we're just supposed
to sit here

00:37:18.262 --> 00:37:19.229
and let this thing kill us?!

00:37:19.263 --> 00:37:20.560
I must point out

00:37:20.597 --> 00:37:23.532
that at least one attempt
we made to reverse the effect...

00:37:23.567 --> 00:37:25.899
the shock pulse...
only made our predicament worse.

00:37:25.936 --> 00:37:28.370
If we continue desperately
improvising solutions,

00:37:28.405 --> 00:37:30.805
our own efforts
may ultimately kill us.

00:37:30.841 --> 00:37:33.366
On the other hand,
there is no definitive evidence

00:37:33.410 --> 00:37:35.935
to suggest that doing nothing
will result in death.

00:37:36.046 --> 00:37:39.277
It's... talking... to... me!

00:37:39.316 --> 00:37:41.284
Do nothing.

00:37:41.318 --> 00:37:43.445
Captain, please lie down.

00:37:43.487 --> 00:37:45.478
What about the Captain?

00:37:45.522 --> 00:37:46.750
She's dying.

00:37:46.790 --> 00:37:48.382
We do not know that.

00:37:48.425 --> 00:37:50.359
At the moment,
she is merely delirious.

00:37:50.394 --> 00:37:53.295
Chakotay, you're in charge here.

00:37:53.330 --> 00:37:55.730
Don't you agree
we've got to keep trying?

00:37:55.766 --> 00:37:58.530
Whatever this thing is,
B'Elanna, it's bigger

00:37:58.569 --> 00:38:00.469
and more powerful than we are.

00:38:00.504 --> 00:38:02.734
Maybe...

00:38:02.773 --> 00:38:05.264
maybe this is one bear
we can't wrestle to the ground.

00:38:05.309 --> 00:38:07.777
Maybe like Tuvok says,
there's nothing we can do

00:38:07.811 --> 00:38:09.938
but let it happen
and hope for the best.

00:38:19.289 --> 00:38:21.450
Fine.

00:38:21.491 --> 00:38:23.925
Fine, Chakotay.

00:38:23.961 --> 00:38:26.293
Have it your way.

00:38:34.805 --> 00:38:37.103
Commander Chakotay.

00:38:37.140 --> 00:38:38.607
Yes, Mr. Tuvok?

00:38:38.642 --> 00:38:41.839
I want to thank you
for endorsing my recommendation.

00:38:41.879 --> 00:38:45.940
You know, Tuvok, I may not get
another chance to say this.

00:38:45.983 --> 00:38:49.146
Sometimes I find you
arrogant and irritating,

00:38:49.186 --> 00:38:51.518
but you're a hell of an officer.

00:38:51.555 --> 00:38:55.457
Thank you, sir, and since
we are speaking candidly,

00:38:55.492 --> 00:38:57.585
may I say, sir,
that I have not always been

00:38:57.628 --> 00:38:59.789
particularly partial
to your methods either.

00:38:59.830 --> 00:39:01.889
I suppose it must
have been tough for you

00:39:01.932 --> 00:39:04.696
to accept my being elevated
to First Officer over you.

00:39:04.735 --> 00:39:07.727
I have always respected
Captain Janeway's decisions.

00:39:07.771 --> 00:39:10.604
However, I suppose
that particular decision

00:39:10.641 --> 00:39:13.735
did put me in a position
I am unaccustomed to.

00:39:13.777 --> 00:39:16.746
If that ever caused me to make
things more difficult for you,

00:39:16.780 --> 00:39:18.611
I must apologize.

00:39:33.964 --> 00:39:36.125
Can I ask you a question?

00:39:36.166 --> 00:39:38.760
Fire away, Harry.

00:39:38.802 --> 00:39:40.793
Are you afraid?

00:39:42.639 --> 00:39:45.267
I chose this life,

00:39:45.309 --> 00:39:49.609
and I guess I always knew
it could come to this...

00:39:49.646 --> 00:39:53.480
but, yeah, I'm afraid.

00:39:56.653 --> 00:39:58.280
Me, too.

00:39:58.322 --> 00:39:59.789
I'm so worried about Neelix.

00:39:59.823 --> 00:40:02.291
I should be with him.

00:40:02.326 --> 00:40:07.127
As much as he may...
annoy me at times,

00:40:07.164 --> 00:40:10.133
Mr. Neelix is one
of the most resourceful

00:40:10.167 --> 00:40:13.625
and resilient individuals
I know.

00:40:13.670 --> 00:40:18.664
If anyone can survive
this calamity, he can.

00:40:42.366 --> 00:40:44.027
Hi.

00:40:45.702 --> 00:40:46.999
Hi.

00:40:47.104 --> 00:40:49.338
What are you doing?

00:40:51.039 --> 00:40:53.371
I'm trying to contact
my spirit guide.

00:40:53.408 --> 00:40:55.501
Why?

00:40:55.544 --> 00:40:59.207
Who knows what's going to happen
when that ring hits us?

00:40:59.247 --> 00:41:01.272
We might be in
for another long journey.

00:41:04.152 --> 00:41:05.744
I guess I could use

00:41:05.787 --> 00:41:09.154
a little spiritual guidance
myself right now.

00:41:09.191 --> 00:41:11.056
You mind if I join you?

00:41:11.093 --> 00:41:14.290
I thought you'd never ask.

00:42:46.188 --> 00:42:47.519
Captain?

00:42:52.027 --> 00:42:53.324
I'm all right.

00:42:53.361 --> 00:42:56.489
You were delirious.

00:42:56.531 --> 00:42:59.159
It was...

00:42:59.201 --> 00:43:00.896
some sort of message.

00:43:00.936 --> 00:43:03.029
What was?

00:43:03.071 --> 00:43:06.131
The spatial distortion.

00:43:07.976 --> 00:43:09.944
It was...

00:43:09.978 --> 00:43:12.845
trying to communicate with us.

00:43:16.818 --> 00:43:19.685
I want a full systems report,

00:43:19.721 --> 00:43:22.815
and Mr. Kim, Mr. Tuvok,
I want every iota of information

00:43:22.858 --> 00:43:25.292
that was recorded
regarding that phenomenon.

00:43:25.327 --> 00:43:27.625
The distortion ring
is directly ahead, Captain.

00:43:27.662 --> 00:43:30.096
It's moving away from us
at 2,000 kph.

00:43:30.131 --> 00:43:32.656
We've got a full crew
complement, Captain.

00:43:32.701 --> 00:43:33.793
No injuries reported.

00:43:33.835 --> 00:43:35.962
No damage to the hull
or ship's systems.

00:43:36.004 --> 00:43:38.131
Incredible.

00:43:38.173 --> 00:43:40.141
You're not going
to believe this, Captain,

00:43:40.175 --> 00:43:42.803
but 20 million gigaquads
of new information

00:43:42.844 --> 00:43:44.971
have been input
into the ship's computer.

00:43:45.013 --> 00:43:46.981
Where did it come from?

00:43:47.015 --> 00:43:50.473
My guess is, it came
from the distortion ring.

00:43:50.519 --> 00:43:52.987
Somebody's definitely trying
to tell us something.

00:43:53.021 --> 00:43:54.648
That's not all, Captain.

00:43:54.689 --> 00:43:57.317
Our entire database has been
copied and downloaded

00:43:57.359 --> 00:43:59.327
into somebody else's system.

00:43:59.361 --> 00:44:00.953
I guess whoever they were,

00:44:00.996 --> 00:44:03.430
they want to know everything
they can about us, too.

00:44:03.465 --> 00:44:09.461
Maybe it was their only way
of communicating with us.

00:44:09.504 --> 00:44:11.938
Maybe...

00:44:11.973 --> 00:44:15.568
they were just trying
to say "hello."

00:44:15.610 --> 00:44:16.736
Cake anyone?

00:44:16.778 --> 00:44:18.803
Neelix, what happened to you?

00:44:18.847 --> 00:44:20.781
Oh, it's a long story.

00:44:20.815 --> 00:44:23.613
I'll tell you
all about it later.

00:44:23.652 --> 00:44:26.450
Right now, it's time
to finish your party.

00:44:26.488 --> 00:44:29.286
Neelix, I need
a photograph of you.

00:44:29.324 --> 00:44:30.586
What for, sweetie?

00:44:30.625 --> 00:44:32.957
From now on,
even when we're separated,

00:44:32.994 --> 00:44:35.724
I want to have you where
I can keep an eye on you.

00:44:37.265 --> 00:44:39.096
Happy birthday, Kes.
